# Math notation (Cursor chat)

When writing mathematical formulas, always use `\(...\)` for inline math and `\[...\]` for block math. Never use `$...$` or `$$...$$` for inline math.

Examples:
- Inline: `\(I(Z;Y)\)`, `\(I(X;Z)\)`, not `$I(Z;Y)$`
- Block: `\[I(X;T) \text{ vs. } I(T;Y)\]`

Avoid nesting math delimiters (e.g. never `\(` inside `\[...\]`).
